course: dictionary
lesson: 12414
title: Dank and gloomy
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Dank is a describing word. «The cellar was dank, and water dripped down the walls.» The dripping water and the cold tell you the cellar is wet and unpleasant.
explain: Dank means unpleasantly cold, wet and stale-smelling. Stale means the air smells old and never moves. Check it: put «cold, wet and stale-smelling» into the sentence instead of dank. It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: «The dungeon smelled dank, and a rat scurried into the shadows.» Writers choose dank to show that a place is uncomfortable and maybe frightening. In stories, dank usually describes a gloomy, damp place such as a cave, a cellar or an old tunnel.
fact: Dank means unpleasantly cold, wet and stale-smelling.
fact: «Dank» is often used for gloomy dungeons, caves, cellars and old tunnels.
fact: Dank places can grow mould, because damp air is the kind of place where mould grows.
fact: Dank is an adjective: danker means more dank, and dankest means the most dank.
fact: In slang, «dank» (mostly US, used by young people) means excellent or cool, and is often used jokingly online.
exercise: «The cellar was dank and cold, with water dripping from the walls.» What does dank mean here? | *Unpleasantly cold, wet and stale-smelling | Brightly lit with lots of windows | Warm and sunny | Full of happy music
exercise: Mia says, «That new game is so dank!» In her slang, what does dank mean? | Dirty and broken | *Excellent and cool | Unpleasantly damp | Very dark and gloomy
exercise: «The cave was dank, so mould grew on the rocks.» Why did mould grow? | The cave had too many windows | Mould is a kind of bird | *The place was damp and wet | The rocks were hot and dry
test: «Deep in the castle, the dank dungeon had no windows.» Which word is closest in meaning to dank? | Tall and thin | *Cold and damp | Noisy and busy | Bright and warm
test: Which word fits the gap? «The cave was even ___ than the cellar.» | dankly | dank-ness | *danker | dankest
exam: Which sentence uses dank in the slang sense? | *Mia said, "That new game is dank, it's so cool!" | The tunnel was dank and dark. | The cellar was dank and smelled of mould. | The rain made the path dank.
